      "id": "claim_2ba206e7e4954b948a6876b596d172fc",
      "statement": "Authorization is capability-based: open() computes the effective role and hands back the full OverseerClientInterface for build/owner or the restricted UseOverseerInterface for use, which implements the entire Overseer interface and throws Unauthorized outside the use allowlist (with inert console-log/action subscriptions), so newly added interface methods fail to compile until deliberately allowed — default-deny by type system.",
