      "id": "claim_005a4f12c72141a2838d4f720fd89725",
      "statement": "Share links encode a secret key in a #share=<key> URL fragment; the raw key is shown once at mint and never stored server-side — only its HMAC-SHA-256 (with a fixed domain-separation key) is stored; a link owns multiple keys where later copies are alias rows pointing at the link id, redemption adds a shareKey edge pointing at the link (all keys collapse to one grant), and a revoked link is unredeemable like an unknown key.",
      "evidence": [
