    {
      "id": "claim_2ba60d1c0d264e67be8c778c5e438b3d",
      "statement": "Revocation is lazy: removing a collaborator severs only the edges granting them access (their record retained even when empty, edges where they are the sharer untouched) and revoking a link sets its revoked flag rather than deleting it; nothing cascades — dependents who lose their only path become unreachable and are denied at open() — and because the graph is never destructively pruned, revocation is reversible by re-adding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L107-L131",
